` THE NEW KINDS OF FISH. three cards each put a new kind of thing on the board. each one is a kind of
` fish like any other: it has a picture, it can be swapped, and three of it in a row pop. load_textures,
` in fish_routines, loads the pictures right after the first seven fish, so that they are fish 8, 9 and 10.
global TEX_JELLY
global TEX_RAY
global TEX_BOTTLE

` JELLIES. with the "jellies" card, some of the new fish that drop in are jellyfish. when a jellyfish
` pops, every fish right next to it has a chance of its own to get stung, and a fish that is stung
` goes belly up. a belly up fish pops when the cursor comes to it, the same as with "bottoms up".
` getRandomValue and stingJelly, in fish_funcs, do it.
` a fish that is belly up already can be stung again, and a second sting turns it into a skeleton. see
` SKELETONS, further down. so can a fish that is next to two jellyfish that pop together, or next to a
` stacked one, which stings once for every jellyfish in the stack. a skeleton is not stung again.
` every sting that lands sends a little bolt from the jellyfish to the fish. see ZAPS.
` the card can be taken more than once. the first card makes JELLY_SPAWN_CHANCE new fish in a hundred
` jellyfish, and every card after it raises that by JELLY_SPAWN_STEP. so it goes 10, 15, 20. the "rays"
` card works the same way, and the two water each other down: the chance of a kind is cut to the share
` that its cards are of all the jellyfish and stingray cards that are owned. so three "jellies" cards make
` 20 new fish in a hundred jellyfish, and one "rays" card on top of that brings it down to 15, with 2 in
` a hundred a stingray. getJellyChance and getRayChance, in fish_routines_ability, work it out.
global JELLY_SPAWN_CHANCE = 10 `how many new fish in a hundred are jellyfish, with the first card
global JELLY_SPAWN_STEP = 5 `how much every card after the first adds to that
global JELLY_MAX = 3 `how many times the card can be taken
global dim STING_DELAY(400) `for every jellyfish that is popping, how long it is until it pops, in milliseconds. the bolts wait for that.
global JELLY_STING_CHANCE = 50 `how many fish in a hundred get stung, of the ones next to a jellyfish that pops

` RAYS. with the "rays" card, some of the new fish are stingrays. whenever a stingray pops, for whatever
` reason, it swims off the way that it is facing, and every fish in its column on that side of it pops
` too, as one group. a stingray faces up, so the fish above it pop, from the stingray to the top. one
` that is belly up faces down, so the fish below it pop, from the stingray to the bottom. landing on
` the bottom row does nothing by itself. handle_combos, in fish_routines, calls shootRay, in
` fish_funcs, for every stingray that is popping.
` the card can be taken more than once, and "jellies" cards water it down. see JELLIES. the first card
` makes RAY_SPAWN_CHANCE new fish in a hundred stingrays, and every card after it raises that by
` RAY_SPAWN_STEP. so it goes 10, 15, 20.
global RAY_SPAWN_CHANCE = 10 `how many new fish in a hundred are stingrays, with the first card
global RAY_SPAWN_STEP = 5 `how much every card after the first adds to that
global RAY_MAX = 3 `how many times the card can be taken

` BOTTLES. with the "bottles" card, a group of fish that matched, and that is big enough, leaves a
` bottle behind, in the cell of the group that is closest to the middle of it. the bottle falls like a
` fish does, and it can be swapped like one. when it is on the bottom row, it adds to the multiplier,
` and it is gone. handle_combos leaves the bottle, and checkBottles, in fish_funcs, pays it out.
global BOTTLE_GROUP_SIZE = 5 `how many fish a group needs to leave a bottle
global BOTTLE_MULT_GAIN = 1 `how much a bottle adds to the multiplier

` ZAPS. little bolts of lightning that jump from one spot on the board to another, and are gone again.
` the top of fish_routines_zap explains how they work.
global ZAP_COUNT = 16 `how many there can be at once
global ZAP_PIECES = 4 `how many pieces a bolt is made of. every piece goes along, and then jogs to the side.
global ZAP_BARS = 8 `how many sprites that takes, which is two for every piece
global ZAP_LIFE = 260 `how long a bolt lasts, in milliseconds
global ZAP_FLICKER_MS = 45 `how long it is before the jogs are picked again
global ZAP_JOG = 4 `how far to the side a jog can go, in pixels
global ZAP_THICK = 2 `how thick the bars are, in pixels
global ZAP_NEXT = 0 `the one that the next bolt takes
global ZAP_LIVE = 0 `how many are showing, or waiting to
global dim ZAP_ACTIVE(16)
global dim ZAP_START_MS(16)
global dim ZAP_FROM_X(16)
global dim ZAP_FROM_Y(16)
global dim ZAP_TO_X(16)
global dim ZAP_TO_Y(16)
global dim ZAP_FLICKER(16) `which set of jogs each one is showing
global dim ZAP_SPRITES(128)

` THE WASTE BUCKET. a special move that pops every belly up fish on the board at once, as one group,
` and they score WASTE_BUCKET_BONUS times as much. it never has to recharge, but it does count as a move.
` it takes every skeleton too. see SKELETONS.
` when there are no belly up fish and no skeletons, it does nothing, and it is not a move. doWasteBucket, in fish_funcs, does it.
global WASTE_BUCKET_BONUS = 2

` BUNCH UP. a special move that is a swap. the fish that the swap connects do not pop. they all go
` into a stack behind the fish that was swapped, and the cells that they leave fill back in. a stack
` made this way can be taller than the cards can make one, up to BUNCH_STACK_MAX, though only the
` first few show. a swap that connects nothing is still a swap. doBunchUp, in fish_funcs, does it.
global BUNCH_STACK_MAX = 9 `the saved game has room for one digit
global BUNCH_UP_COOLDOWN = 2 `this counts the move itself, so there is one move to wait

` FORCED POPS. a cell with a comboForce pops the next time that handle_combos looks at the board, no
` matter what is in it, and the cells that have the same number pop as one group. these are the numbers.
` 1 is a belly up fish that the cursor came to.
global FORCE_BUCKET = 2 `the belly up fish of the waste bucket, which score more
global FORCE_BUNCH = 3 `fish that are going into a stack. they go away without popping, and score nothing.
global FORCE_RAY = 10 `the fish above a stingray that popped. the column is added to this.
global FORCE_BOTTLE = 40 `a bottle that paid out. the column is added to this too.
global FORCE_RAY_DOWN = 70 `the fish below a belly up stingray that popped. the column is added to this too.

` THE ROBOT. a special move that makes swaps for the player. it looks at the fish near the cursor, picks
` the swap that would pop the most fish, makes it, and then does that again, a few times over.
` the swaps do not count as moves of their own, and they do not touch the multiplier. the whole thing
` counts as the one move. doRobot, in fish_funcs, does it.
global ROBOT_SWAPS = 3 `how many swaps it makes
global ROBOT_REACH = 2 `how many cells away from the cursor it looks, in every direction
global ROBOT_COOLDOWN = 2 `how many moves it takes to recharge
global ROBOT_SWAP_TIME = 170 `how long each of its swaps takes, in milliseconds
global ROBOT_STAMP = 1000000 `a number that is different for every search that it makes. see robotGroupSize.
global ROBOT_LAST_COUNT = 0 `how many swaps it made the last time. 0 means that it found nothing to do.

` KNOWN FILL. a special move that is a swap. when the swap pops fish, the new fish that drop in to
` fill the gaps are all the same kind as the fish that was moved, instead of being picked at random.
` that only goes for the first time the board fills back in. if those fish pop in turn, what fills in
` after them is picked at random again, or it would never stop.
` a bottle is not copied this way. the move cannot be used on a swap that has a bottle in it, on
` either side. it is turned down, and it is not used up. process_input, in fish_routines_input, does that.
` doKnownFill, in fish_funcs, starts it, and handle_combos does the filling.
global KNOWN_FILL_COOLDOWN = 4 `how many moves it takes to recharge
global KNOWN_FILL_VALUE = 0 `the kind of fish that the next fill is made of, or 0 when it is picked at random

