` THE HINTS. now and then something small goes along the shape of a pattern that is out, somewhere on the
` board: a couple of bubbles come up from the cell at one end of it, then a patch of the water goes calm,
` and the calm moves slowly from cell to cell along the pattern, and a couple more bubbles come up from the
` cell at the other end. all of the water wobbles all of the time, and has ripples of light in it. in the
` patch it is still and clear. and the specks that are drifting behind the board anyway glow as they
` pass through where it is. the screen effect does the calm, and the specks effect does the specks.
` over coral the water hardly moves, so there is no calm to see, and the specks are lost against the rock.
` so there, the specks glow a lot more, and the coral itself lights up where the hint is passing: the
` rock, and the things that grow on it. the coral effect does that.
` it is meant to be easy to miss, and hard to miss once it has been noticed.
` which pattern it is, where on the board, and which end it starts from, is picked at random every time.
` none of those matter. only the shape does, because a pattern can be walked from either end.
` it happens on its own every so often: when a wave of the current sets out, there is a chance of one. and
` a big group of fish that pops always brings one, as soon as the board has settled.

` LISTEN. with the "listen" card, a hint is a lot easier to see. the specks glow brighter, and further out
` from where it is, and it leaves a trail of light behind it, along the path that it took, which fades
` and thins the further back it is, and bends where it turned. CORAL_HINT_TRAIL# is the path, for the specks
` effect to draw it. a hint that a big group of fish brought always leaves a trail, and a hint that
` came on its own does CORAL_LISTEN_LUCK times in a hundred, and that is when the name of the card shakes
` in the list of passives. see CORAL_HINT_TRAIL_ON. the
` patch of calm water is bigger. more bubbles come up at each end. and the name of the card shakes in
` the list of passives when a hint starts. it does not make hints come any more often.
global CORAL_LISTEN_GLOW# = 2.2 `how many times as bright the specks glow
global CORAL_LISTEN_REACH# = 1.5 `how many times as far out from the hint they glow
global CORAL_LISTEN_CALM# = 1.4 `how many times as big the patch of calm water is
global CORAL_LISTEN_BUBBLES = 3 `how many more bubbles come up at each end
global CORAL_HINT_GLOW_POWER# = 0 `how strongly the specks glow on this frame. it is CORAL_HINT_POWER#, and more with the card.
global CORAL_HINT_LISTEN# = 0 `1 on a frame that the card is owned, for the specks effect
global dim CORAL_HINT_TRAIL#(16) `eight spots along the path of the hint, from where it is to where it was, each CORAL_HINT_TRAIL_MS before the last, with the corners rounded off. x and then y of each.
global CORAL_HINT_TRAIL_MS = 320
global CORAL_HINT_TRAIL_ON = 0 `1 while the hint that is playing is one that leaves a trail, with the card
global CORAL_LISTEN_LUCK = 10 `how many of the hints that come on their own in a hundred leave a trail too, with the card. nothing says so.

global CORAL_HINT_CHANCE = 30 `how many waves of the current in a hundred bring a hint
global CORAL_HINT_GROUP_SIZE = 5 `a group of this many fish that pops always brings one
global CORAL_HINT_STEP_MS = 900 `how long it takes to get from one cell to the next, in milliseconds
global CORAL_HINT_FADE_MS = 450 `how long it takes to swell up at the start, and to die away at the end
global CORAL_HINT_TAIL_MS = 450 `the specks glow this far behind it
global CORAL_HINT_BUBBLES = 2 `how many bubbles come up at each end
global CORAL_HINT_BULGE# = 1.3 `how wide the patch of calm water is, in cells, from the middle of it to the edge
global CORAL_HINT_REACH# = .75 `and how far from it the specks glow, the same way
global CORAL_HINT_ROLLED = -1 `the last wave of the current that has had its roll for a hint
global CORAL_HINT_DUE = 0 `1 when a hint is owed, for a big group of fish that popped
global CORAL_HINT_SLOT = -1 `the slot of the pattern that the hint is for
global CORAL_HINT_START_MS = -1 `when the hint that is playing started, or -1 if none is
global CORAL_HINT_COUNT = 0 `how many cells it goes over
global dim CORAL_HINT_X(16) `the cells, in the order that it goes over them
global dim CORAL_HINT_Y(16)
global CORAL_HINT_POINT_X# = 0 `where coralHintPointAt worked out that it is, in pixels of the game
global CORAL_HINT_POINT_Y# = 0
global CORAL_HINT_POWER# = 0 `how strong the hint is on this frame, from 0 to 1
global CORAL_HINT_HEAD_X# = 0 `where it is on this frame, in pixels of the game. updateSeabed tells the specks.
global CORAL_HINT_HEAD_Y# = 0
global CORAL_HINT_TAIL_X# = 0 `and where it was a moment ago
global CORAL_HINT_TAIL_Y# = 0
global CORAL_HINT_GLOW_REACH# = 0 `how far from it the specks glow, in pixels

` where the board is, for the specks effect, which makes the specks of a hint brighter over coral, where
` they are hard to see. stepCoral keeps these up, and updateSeabed hands them on.
global CORAL_FX_LEFT# = 0 `the top left corner of the board, in pixels of the game
global CORAL_FX_TOP# = 0
global CORAL_FX_CELL# = 0 `how big a cell is
global CORAL_FX_COLUMNS = 0
global CORAL_FX_ROWS = 0

